          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Jacques-Louis David's Early Life</strong><br>\nJacques-Louis David was born in Paris in 1748 and trained under rococo painters before becoming a supporter of the neoclassical style, reflecting the ideals of the Enlightenment through his emphasis on morality and virtue in his works.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Role in the French Revolution</strong><br>\nDavid's artistic talents aligned with his political activities. A member of the radical Jacobin group, he became an active supporter of the French Revolution and later a friend of Napoleon, using his art as a means of political expression.</p>\n\n<p><strong>\"The Oath of the Horatii\"</strong><br>\nIn 1784, David painted \"The Oath of the Horatii,\" which became a manifesto for the neoclassical movement. The work emphasizes stoicism and sacrifice for the greater good, mirroring revolutionary values.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
